menu "cli_web: browser transport for the shell"

    config CLI_WEB_MAX_OPEN_SOCKETS
        int "Maximum simultaneous HTTP sockets"
        default 7
        range 2 16
        help
            Every open browser tab holds a WebSocket for as long as it is on the
            page, so the httpd default of 4 runs out with a couple of tabs. Only
            applied when cli_web starts its own server; a borrowed server keeps
            whatever its owner configured.

    config CLI_WEB_BROADCAST_CHUNK
        int "Maximum bytes per WebSocket frame"
        default 512
        range 128 4096
        help
            Output longer than this is split across frames. Each chunk is
            malloc'd and handed to the server task, so larger values mean fewer,
            bigger allocations.

    config CLI_WEB_MAX_COMMAND_LEN
        int "Maximum command length accepted from a browser (bytes)"
        default 512
        range 64 2048
        help
            Frames longer than this are ignored rather than truncated: a command
            cut in half is more dangerous than one that never ran.

endmenu
